you guys were moving to New York.

759
01:10:50,530 --> 01:10:52,910
Thanks for telling me.

760
01:10:53,030 --> 01:10:55,580
We weren't all gonna move.

761
01:10:56,790 --> 01:10:58,750
Oh.

762
01:11:00,710 --> 01:11:04,040
I let the answering machine
pick up the other call.

763
01:11:08,170 --> 01:11:10,130
Great.

764
01:11:21,690 --> 01:11:25,440
Look, let'sjust be honest here.
We're just at the beginning...

765
01:11:25,570 --> 01:11:28,570
and I don't expect
you or I to change...

766
01:11:28,650 --> 01:11:31,110
the course of where
our lives were headed...

767
01:11:31,200 --> 01:11:33,490
because of one date.

768
01:11:33,570 --> 01:11:38,040
And if you do go to New York,
we can develop this.

769
01:11:38,120 --> 01:11:41,290
We'll just be forced to take it slow.

770
01:11:41,370 --> 01:11:45,130
And in the end, I think
that's defiinitely better.

771
01:11:47,670 --> 01:11:49,960
I mean, this is our second time around,
David. I didn't expect us...

772
01:11:50,050 --> 01:11:52,340
to get carried away.

773
01:11:54,590 --> 01:11:58,430
But I guess "congratulations"
is the right thing to say.

774
01:12:23,250 --> 01:12:25,460
David, it's Elijah.

775
01:12:25,580 --> 01:12:27,540
It was so obvious.

776
01:12:27,670 --> 01:12:29,960
It was this one issue
that brought it back for me--

777
01:12:30,090 --> 01:12:32,050
Century Comics 117.

778
01:12:32,170 --> 01:12:34,300
That's where this group,
the Coalition of Evil...

779
01:12:34,380 --> 01:12:36,840
tried to ascertain the weakness
of every superhero...

780
01:12:36,970 --> 01:12:40,390
because they all have one,
just like you.

781
01:12:40,470 --> 01:12:44,520
Your bones don't break.
Mine do. That's clear.

782
01:12:44,600 --> 01:12:48,020
Your cells react to bacteria
and viruses differently than mine.

783
01:12:48,150 --> 01:12:52,070
You don't get sick.
I do. That's also clear.

784
01:12:52,190 --> 01:12:57,490
But for some reason, you and I
react the exact same way to water.

785
01:12:57,570 --> 01:12:59,950
We swallow it too fast, we choke.

786
01:13:00,080 --> 01:13:02,290
We get some in our lungs, we drown.

787
01:13:02,410 --> 01:13:07,460
However unreal it may seem,
we are connected, you and I.

788
01:13:07,580 --> 01:13:12,210
We're on the same curve,
just on opposite ends.

789
01:13:12,340 --> 01:13:16,380
The point of all this is we
now know something we didn't.

790
01:13:16,470 --> 01:13:19,970
You have a weakness-- water.

791
01:13:20,100 --> 01:13:23,020
It's like your kryptonite.

792
01:13:23,140 --> 01:13:25,440
You hearing me, David?

793
01:15:40,400 --> 01:15:42,360
Audrey?

794
01:16:15,810 --> 01:16:18,190
Gotcha. Come on.

795
01:16:35,830 --> 01:16:38,670
Audrey. Audrey.

796
01:16:44,550 --> 01:16:46,510
Hey!

797
01:16:50,640 --> 01:16:53,480
You'll be okay.

798
01:16:53,600 --> 01:16:57,360
What-- What happened?

799
01:16:57,480 --> 01:17:01,400
I thought I was--
I thought I was dead.

800
01:17:01,480 --> 01:17:03,440
Me too.

801
01:17:07,950 --> 01:17:09,910
Is she all right?

802
01:17:10,030 --> 01:17:12,330
I think her leg's broken.

803
01:17:12,450 --> 01:17:15,000
Are you hurt?

804
01:17:15,080 --> 01:17:17,290
Hey, man, are you hurt?

805
01:17:47,740 --> 01:17:49,700
Hello.

806
01:17:49,820 --> 01:17:52,580
I wasn't injured in that caraccident.

807
01:17:52,660 --> 01:17:55,290
David.

808
01:17:55,370 --> 01:17:57,920
I've never been injured, Eliijah.

809
01:18:00,250 --> 01:18:02,550
What am I supposed to do?

810
01:18:08,510 --> 01:18:11,350
Go to where people are.

811
01:18:11,470 --> 01:18:14,470
You won't have to look very long.

812
01:18:16,100 --> 01:18:19,020
It's all right to be afraid, David...

813
01:18:19,150 --> 01:18:23,190
because this part won't be
like a comic book.

814
01:18:23,270 --> 01:18:28,150
Real life doesn't fit into little boxes
that were drawn for it.

815
01:19:06,480 --> 01:19:10,410
There's one in the first row.
It's-- It's the second one.

816
01:19:10,530 --> 01:19:13,370
Yes. It's the second one over.

817
01:19:46,570 --> 01:19:48,690
Go back to Africa!

818
01:20:05,040 --> 01:20:07,250
Hey, what's your name?

819
01:20:12,930 --> 01:20:15,140
I think you drank too much.

820
01:21:00,770 --> 01:21:02,810
Can I come in?

821
01:21:02,890 --> 01:21:05,440
Who are you?

822
01:21:05,520 --> 01:21:08,270
I like your house.

823
01:21:08,400 --> 01:21:10,360
Can I come in?

824
01:21:10,480 --> 01:21:12,690
What is this?

825
01:21:14,360 --> 01:21:17,620
No, you can't come in.

826
01:21:17,740 --> 01:21:20,200
Are you sure?

827
01:21:20,280 --> 01:21:22,580
What are-- What are you--

828
01:25:52,770 --> 01:25:54,730
It's okay.

829
01:26:05,110 --> 01:26:07,070
It's okay. It's okay.

830
01:32:50,810 --> 01:32:53,350
I had a bad dream.

831
01:32:59,280 --> 01:33:01,400
It's over now.

832
01:33:29,430 --> 01:33:32,270
I don't know.

833
01:33:32,350 --> 01:33:34,390
I can't believe you'd think that.

834
01:33:34,520 --> 01:33:36,480
I'm just asking you.

835
01:33:39,770 --> 01:33:41,980
I'm making French toast.

836
01:33:57,420 --> 01:33:59,960
I've been thinking about Elijah Price.

837
01:34:01,300 --> 01:34:05,050
If he shows up again, I think
we should call the police, okay?

838
01:34:09,180 --> 01:34:11,140
Okay?

839
01:34:13,680 --> 01:34:15,640
Okay.

840
01:35:23,800 --> 01:35:25,840
You were right.

841
01:36:15,470 --> 01:36:19,520
This is one of Johann Davis'
earliest drawings.

842
01:36:19,640 --> 01:36:22,020
See the villain's eyes?

843
01:36:22,100 --> 01:36:24,310
They're larger than
the other characters'.

844
01:36:24,440 --> 01:36:29,940
They insinuate a slightly skewed
perspective on how they see the world--

845
01:36:31,070 --> 01:36:33,360
just off normal.

846
01:36:33,450 --> 01:36:35,740
He doesn't look scary.

847
01:36:35,870 --> 01:36:38,330
Mm-hmm. That's what I said to my son.

848
01:36:38,450 --> 01:36:41,120
But he says there's always two kinds.

849
01:36:41,210 --> 01:36:45,590
There's the soldier villain
who fights the hero with his hands...

850
01:36:45,710 --> 01:36:50,010
and then there's the real threat--
the brilliant and evil archenemy...

851
01:36:50,090 --> 01:36:52,550
who fights the hero with his mind.

852
01:36:52,680 --> 01:36:54,640
Are you Elijah's mother?

853
01:36:54,760 --> 01:36:58,510
I am. I'm helping him with the sale.

854
01:36:58,600 --> 01:37:01,350
Nice to meet you. I'm David Dunn.

855
01:37:01,480 --> 01:37:03,440
He's spoken ofyou.

856
01:37:03,560 --> 01:37:05,520
Says you're becoming friends.

857
01:37:05,650 --> 01:37:08,020
We are.

858
01:37:08,150 --> 01:37:10,360
Looks like he's doing good today.

859
01:37:11,490 --> 01:37:14,410
I'm very proud of him.

860
01:37:14,490 --> 01:37:17,580
He's come through a lot in his life--

861
01:37:17,660 --> 01:37:21,160
a couple of bad spills
I thought had broken him.

862
01:37:21,290 --> 01:37:24,370
Mm-hmm. They were bad...

863
01:37:25,540 --> 01:37:28,090
but he made it.

864
01:37:28,170 --> 01:37:30,130
Yes, he did.

865
01:37:31,300 --> 01:37:33,510
He's kind of a miracle.

866
01:37:35,680 --> 01:37:37,640
Yes, he is.

867
01:37:41,220 --> 01:37:43,890
- I'll tell him you're here.
- Thank you.

868
01:37:45,230 --> 01:37:48,980
We'll work something out.
Always able to work something out.

869
01:38:14,050 --> 01:38:16,010
It has begun.

870
01:38:19,180 --> 01:38:21,310
Tell me something, David.

871
01:38:22,430 --> 01:38:26,980
When you woke up this morning,
was it still there?

872
01:38:27,060 --> 01:38:29,900
The sadness?

873
01:38:30,020 --> 01:38:31,980
No.

874
01:38:35,610 --> 01:38:38,610
I think this is where we shake hands.

875
01:38:57,680 --> 01:39:00,680
- Look!
- Did you see it?

876
01:39:10,100 --> 01:39:12,570
I worked in that building 25 years.

877
01:39:12,690 --> 01:39:14,820
I know all its secrets.

878
01:39:16,280 --> 01:39:18,240
Secrets?

879
01:39:19,700 --> 01:39:24,580
Like if there ever was a fire
on floors one, two or three...

880
01:39:24,700 --> 01:39:28,210
everyone in that hotel
would be burned alive.

881
01:39:34,170 --> 01:39:36,920
Passengers aren't allowed in there.

882
01:40:20,220 --> 01:40:22,680
Do you know what
the scariest thing is?

883
01:40:26,390 --> 01:40:29,640
To not know your place
in this world...

884
01:40:29,770 --> 01:40:32,310
to not know why you're here.

885
01:40:33,600 --> 01:40:35,570
That's--

886
01:40:37,440 --> 01:40:39,820
That's just an awful feeling.

887
01:40:41,240 --> 01:40:43,530
What have you done?

888
01:40:44,740 --> 01:40:47,740
I almost gave up hope.

889
01:40:47,870 --> 01:40:51,040
There were so many times
I questioned myself.

890
01:40:51,160 --> 01:40:53,710
You killed all those people.

891
01:40:55,000 --> 01:40:57,840
But I found you.

892
01:40:57,920 --> 01:41:01,170
So many sacrifiices...

893
01:41:02,340 --> 01:41:04,300
just to find you.

894
01:41:04,430 --> 01:41:06,390
Jesus Christ!

895
01:41:16,310 --> 01:41:19,070
Now that we know who you are...

896
01:41:20,230 --> 01:41:22,950
I know who I am.

897
01:41:26,530 --> 01:41:28,740
I'm not a mistake.

898
01:41:30,240 --> 01:41:32,370
It all makes sense.

899
01:41:32,500 --> 01:41:37,040
In a comic, you know how you can tell
who the arch-villain's going to be?

900
01:41:37,170 --> 01:41:40,510
He's the exact opposite of the hero.

901
01:41:40,630 --> 01:41:44,380
And most times, they're friends,
like you and me.

902
01:41:44,470 --> 01:41:48,300
I should've known way back when.
You know why, David?

903
01:41:48,390 --> 01:41:50,350
Because of the kids.

904
01:42:00,320 --> 01:42:02,990
They called me Mr. Glass.
